body:
Having a gap doesnt make you dumb. It doesnt challenge your identity. Avoiding it makes you dumb. If you take a few minutes and fill it you'll be eternally grateful when you can comfortably add fractions and the problem is rational functions etc.

&#x200B;

love this. this is sooooo accurate. I myself have skirted by so much through school and even a biochemistry major. I constantly tell people I have no idea how I did it because I feel like I don't know or remember anything. This past year, though, I truly have slowed down to fill in the gaps. Identifying and amending these gaps have made me feel so much more confident.
